---

## Maintenance Policy

- Update `rules_version` when material policy changes occur.
- Reflect change in `CHANGELOG.md` under “Policy Updates”.
- Review `.rules` quarterly or upon major architectural expansion.

---

## Prohibited Actions

| Action | Reason |
|--------|--------|
| Manual release tag creation | Breaks reproducibility & CI audit trail |
| Adding endpoint without bumping MINOR | Violates atomic evolution principle |
| Logging full HTTP bodies | Risk of sensitive data leakage |
| Skipping acceptance tests for a resource | Undermines lifecycle reliability |
| Hardcoding secrets in tests | Security violation |
| Silent retries without logging | Observability gap |
| Suppressing lint warnings without comment | Reduces code quality accountability |

---

## Policy Change Workflow

1. Propose change in PR description.
2. Update `.rules` + `CLAUDE.md` anchors if design rationale impacted.
3. Bump `rules_version`.
4. Update CHANGELOG (“Policy Changes” section).
5. Obtain at least one maintainer approval before merge.

---

## Final Notes

- Keep implementation lean; policy solely defines guard rails.
- Policy drift must be minimized—CI should fail on divergence (automation recommended).
- Agents parse frontmatter keys for automated reasoning; keep stable key names.

## User-Facing Documentation Policy

This section defines normative rules for maintaining user-facing documentation in the mdBook (`docs/`) without duplicating internal policy or generated schema reference.

### Layering

| Layer | Location | Audience | Content |
|-------|----------|----------|---------|
| Policies (normative must/shall) | `.rules` | Contributors / automation | Operational constraints |
| Design rationale (why) | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Contributors | Architectural & modeling decisions |
| Execution workflow (how) | `.claude/AGENT_CHECKLIST.md` | Contributors / agents | Stepwise implementation |
| Troubleshooting (dev) | `.claude/FAQ.md` | Contributors | Internal pitfalls & resolutions |
| Generated schema docs | (terraform-plugin-docs output) | Users | Argument & attribute reference tables |
| Narrative user docs | `docs/` (mdBook) | Users | Concepts, architecture, versioning, security, pagination, retry, observability, migrations |

### Triggers Requiring mdBook Update

| Trigger | Required mdBook Action |
|---------|------------------------|
| New resource | Add/extend page under `docs/src/resources/<resource>.md`; update navigation |
| New data source | Add page under `docs/src/data-sources/<data_source>.md` |
| New pagination capability (e.g. `all`, `limit`) | Update pagination concept page |
| Retry/backoff policy change | Update retry concept page |
| Security / sensitive handling change | Update security concept page |
| Observability phase advancement | Update observability page |
| Breaking change (MAJOR) | Add migration guide `docs/src/migrations/<major>.md` |
| Deprecation removal | Update migration guide + affected concept pages |
| Importer feature added | Add / update importers or resource usage guidance |

### Directory Conventions

| Area | Path Pattern |
|------|--------------|
| Concept guides | `docs/src/concepts/<topic>.md` |
| Resources | `docs/src/resources/<resource>.md` |
| Data sources | `docs/src/data-sources/<data_source>.md` |
| Migrations | `docs/src/migrations/<major>.md` |
| Generated reference (linked, not duplicated) | `docs/src/generated/` |

### Content Rules

- Do NOT copy full attribute tables into mdBook; link to generated provider docs.
- Concept pages focus on behavior, lifecycle semantics, upgrade/migration guidance, and usage patterns.
- README stays a concise landing (install, quick start, links to mdBook & registry).
- Migration guides appear only for MAJOR versions.

### PR Acceptance Criteria (Documentation Aspect)

A PR introducing any trigger above MUST:
1. Modify or add the corresponding mdBook page(s).
2. Update `SUMMARY.md` navigation if a new page is added.
3. Ensure no stale references to removed/renamed attributes remain.
4. Reference the CHANGELOG entry describing the change.

If no mdBook change is required, the PR description MUST briefly justify (e.g., “PATCH: internal refactor, no user-visible change”).

### CI / Automation Recommendations

- Detect new files under `internal/resource/` or `internal/data/` → enforce presence of matching `docs/src/resources/` or `docs/src/data-sources/` page delta.
- On MAJOR version bump → require a migration guide file.
- Link checker validates all intra-book links.
- Optional: compare generated schema docs vs concept pages to warn on possible duplication (heuristic).

